1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,567
Rule eight. Never follow the voice.
Follow the cord.

2
00:00:04,067 --> 00:00:10,600
We look back at the phone. The cord
isn't cut anymore. It's tight, like a
rope, and it runs through a hole in
the wall.

3
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:14,400
Walt grabs the lantern. I grab the
inhaler. We follow the cord.

4
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:22,767
The cord runs out of the radio room,
across the yard, under the gate. A
black line in the grass, glowing a
little in Walt's lantern light.

5
00:00:23,267 --> 00:00:30,400
Telephone poles. They hung cables on
them once. It leads to the old
exchange. Half a mile. I've never gone
in.

6
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:34,067
Rule nine. Carry a light you can hand
to someone else.
